<title>USA: Texas Utilities, Enserch close deal.</title>
<headline>Texas Utilities, Enserch close deal.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS, Texas 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texas Utilities Co said on Tuesday that it had completed its $1.7 billion merger with Enserch Corp.</p>
<p>The two Dallas-based energy services companies announced their intent to merge on April 15, 1996, but faced a review by the U.S. Department of Justice later in the year.</p>
<p>Under terms of the agreement, Enserch becomes a wholly owned subsidiary of Texas Utilities. The transaction creates an energy services company serving more than 2.8 million customers in north and central Texas, Texas Utilities said in a statement.</p>
</text>
